      "description": "Watch New York Red Bulls vs Orlando City SC highlights and goals from Major League Soccer on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 2, 2026. The Red Bull Arena played host to a frantic Major League Soccer clash on August 2, 2026, as two Eastern Conference rivals went head-to-head in a match defined by clinical finishing and tactical shifts. Both sides pushed their limits in a contest that kept the supporters on the edge of their seats until the final whistle. New York Takes Command The match began with high intensity, and it didn't take long for the New York Red Bulls to find their rhythm. In the 23rd minute, Gustav Berggren delivered a precise ball to Mijahir Jimenez , who made no mistake in slotting it home to give the hosts the lead. The pressure continued as the first half progressed, and just before the interval, Emil Forsberg capitalized on a Cade Cowell assist in the 43rd minute to double the advantage, leaving Orlando City SC with a mountain to climb. A Frantic Second Half The second period saw immediate changes, with Tyrese Spicer entering the fray for Orlando. He made an instant impact, scoring in the 52nd minute following a setup by Braian Ojeda . However, the Red Bulls responded quickly; in the 60th minute, Cade Cowell provided his second assist of the night, allowing Mijahir Jimenez to restore the two-goal cushion with his second strike of the match. Orlando's Resilience and Late Tensions The drama wasn't over, as Griffin Dorsey pulled one back for the visitors in the 63rd minute, assisted by Spicer , making it 3-2. The closing stages were marked by a flurry of tactical substitutions and a rise in tempers. Ivan Angulo , Harvey Sarajian , and Jahkeele Marshall-Rutty all saw yellow cards as the game reached a boiling point. Despite Orlando City SC 's late push through an extended stoppage time, the New York Red Bulls held firm to secure a hard-fought victory."
